From: EglantinePS5
Subject: [PATCH] up: EDEN_UP_TC_AREA_STALE=<MiB>: after an area change, with the pool short, clean images unused for 120 frames go even when costly (ASTC, CPU-decoded, kept as re-made); count lines; off by default

Switches: EDEN_UP_TC_AREA_STALE=<MiB> (1 to 65535, digits only; unset, 0 or anything else: off).
EDEN_UP_TC_AREA_STALE_FRAMES=<frames> (window, unset/0: 1800), _BURST=<images> (unset/0: 400),
_WAVE_MIB=<MiB> (unset/0: 128), _CPU=0 (exact "0": CPU-decoded images stay).
Lines: stderr "EDEN_UP_TC_AREA_STALE open at frame ..." / "... closed at frame ...";
eden_log (HW.GPU) "EDEN_UP_TC_AREA_STALE 600 frames: ..." (deleted by kind, made again).

Why (READ, a hand-played session, its crash log): at census n=405 (t 971 s,
line 8212) the buffers fell 464 -> 16 MiB and the images 1020 -> 612 MiB (the area change before the
load into the area past the field). From n=406 to n=411 (lines 8248-8365, 12 s) 366 MiB of images
sat clean and unused for 120 frames, every byte of it ASTC (stale_clean=366 astc=366), with the
pool's largest free block at 176 MiB and 1,483 MiB free; the load at n=411 then needed ~2,160.
Nothing deleted them:
- 0730 (EDEN_UP_TC_SHORT_COLLECT=1024, in v3.4): "600 frames with the pool under 1024 MiB ... 0
  images" (eden_log 11128). It skips CostlyLoad, and on the console every ASTC texture is CostlyLoad
  (vk_texture_cache.cpp: no ASTC sampling -> Converted + CostlyLoad).
- The collector: images 601 MiB, under its 1024 MiB floor (minimum_memory), so it never ran; above
  it, it skips CostlyLoad until it is past critical.
- AreaEvict: burst 31 at frame 32313 (stderr 7942), done at 32463 with 0 deleted (8088), before
  those images went unused (stale_clean 17 at n=403, 73 at n=404, 377 at n=405).
What did go at that change: 0730 deleted 494 images, 381 MiB, in the 600 frames before eden_log
1044.5 (line 11048; the cheap part of the area left, images 1020 -> 612 at n=404 -> 405), and the
buffer cache fell 463 -> 16 MiB between eden_log 1041.5 and 1042.5 (11013, 11020). The texture
cache counted 600 frames in 10 s there (11048 -> 11128): 1800 frames is 30 s.

What: AreaStaleDrop(), in TickFrame after ShortPoolCollect and before the collector. A window of
_FRAMES frames opens (or is pushed on) on a burst of _BURST new images within 30 frames, or on a
wave: UnmapMemory, AreaEvict and 0730's ShortPoolCollect together deleting _WAVE_MIB of images
within 120 frames (NoteAreaStaleWave; the collector's deletes do not count, it runs under pressure
all through the field). At n=405 the wave was 0730's 381 MiB. While it is open and the pool's largest free block (MemoryCensus::FreeLargest, read
every 30 frames) is under <MiB>, up to 32 images a frame unused for 120 frames
(MemoryCensus::StaleFrames, what the census calls stale) go, oldest first: anything not GPU-written
and not decoding, the costly ones included. Delete reason "area-stale" (not "gc", so
EDEN_UP_TC_KEEP_REMADE does not learn from it). An image made again at a deleted image's address
within the window's length is counted (the drop's cost: an ASTC re-decode on the GPU, a CPU decode
for the two 1365x1365x90 arrays, 4.5 s each in the 13 Nov logs, 321 MiB of heap while both run;
_CPU=0 keeps those two). Off: one test of a static per frame and per unmapped image.

Expected (READ, not run): at n=405 the window opens (0730's 381 MiB came within a few frames:
INFERRED from stale_clean 73 at n=404 and the images 1020 -> 612 two seconds later, 0730 deleting
up to 32 a frame), the pool is under 1024 (largest 20-176), and the 366 MiB go within a few dozen
frames (32 images a frame; their count is not in the census), well before the load at n=411 (12 s,
about 700 frames). What reaches the pool: the images
over half a VMA block (dedicated, EDEN_VMA_BLOCK_MIB=8: over 4 MiB, incl. the two arrays, 84 + 33
MiB, if they were among them: not checked) at once; the smaller ones only as their 8 MiB blocks
empty. Between 117 MiB (the arrays alone) and ~366 + part of the 328 MiB block slack (if those
blocks held mostly these images). Not on the console yet.
Risk: turning back into the field brings each texture back with a re-decode (a frame or a few per
texture; the arrays seconds). The window needs both an area change and a short pool.
Translation id: texture_cache.h and texture_cache_base.h are not in tools/gen-translation-id.py's
inputs (t166c/translation_inputs-7f97.txt, 418 files), and the new names are not in
TranslationSwitches: KEEPS THE STORE.

